  "summary": "Next.js missing cache-control header may lead to CDN caching empty reply",
  "description": "Next.js before 13.4.20-canary.13 lacks a cache-control header and thus empty prefetch responses may sometimes be cached by a CDN, causing a denial of service to all users requesting the same URL via that CDN. Cloudflare considers these requests cacheable assets.",
